  "brief": "Marvell and Lumentum have announced a $115 billion all-stock merger focused on AI data center growth, marking the latest major deal in the tech sector.\n\nMarvell / Lumentum (Announced): Marvell and Lumentum Merger. Marvell and Lumentum have announced a $115 billion merger [1, 2, 3]. The deal is an all-stock transaction [5, 8]. The companies will focus on AI data center growth [6, 7]. The stage of the deal is currently announced [1, 2, 3].\nSkyline / Cove Kaz (Announced): Skyline and Cove Kaz Merger. Skyline and Cove Kaz merger is off [16, 15, 14]. The deal was announced [15]. Funding closure will determine Skyline's share value [14].\nKimberly-Clark / Kenvue (Completed): Kimberly-Clark Acquires Kenvue. Kimberly-Clark has acquired Kenvue, creating the preeminent global consumer health and wellness leader [18, 19, 20]. Kenvue has requested delisting from the NYSE following the acquisition [17]. The acquisition was approved by the EU after a divestment agreement was reached [19].\nNeighborhood Intelligence / tZero (Announced): Neighborhood Intelligence and tZero. Neighborhood Intelligence is merging with tZero [21, 26]. The merger was cancelled [22, 23, 25]. Neighborhood Intelligence is ending its blockchain merger plan [24, 26].\nBuyers Circle / Mark Walter’s F1 Team (Announced): Buyers Circle and F1 Team Deal. Buyers Circle and Mark Walter's F1 team have been acquired [27, 28]. The deal was announced [27]. No further information is available [27].\nPublicis / LiveRamp (Announced): Publicis Acquires LiveRamp. Publicis has acquired LiveRamp, a data hub used by its agency rivals [29, 30]. Publicis is not worried about competitors leaving the deal [30]. The deal is worth $2.2 billion [30].\nThrive Holdings / ADT (Announced): Thrive Holdings and ADT Acquisition. Thrive Holdings is acquiring ADT in a $15.3 billion deal [31, 34, 35]. The acquisition was announced by Thrive Holdings and ADT [32, 33, 36]. The deal is an all-cash transaction [35, 36].\nVusion / In-Store Media (Completed): Vusion and In-Store Media Deal Completed. Vusion has completed its retail media deal with In-Store Media [37]. The deal was announced previously [37].\n\nAlso worth knowing:\n- A class action lawsuit seeks recovery for investors in Compass, Inc. (COMP) with a December 8, 2026 deadline [38].\n- Netanyahu is pressing Trump to attack Iran after the midterms, officials say [39].\n- A South Florida real estate firm was acquired in a $5.2B deal [40].",
